Reason:
When `tpm2_key_decode` allocates a temporary blob (new format, `blob != payload->blob`), the function has multiple early `return` statements that exit before the only cleanup point (`out` label) which frees the blob only if `blob != payload->blob`. These early returns cause the allocated blob to be leaked.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
u8 *blob_ref __free(kfree) = NULL;
```
```
} else {
