    tpm_buf_destroy(&buf);
```
(Removal of `if (blob != payload->blob) kfree(blob);` inside `out:`)
Reason:
The fix introduces a helper variable `blob_ref` with the `__free(kfree)` attribute, which automatically frees the allocated memory when `blob_ref` goes out of scope (i.e., at function exit). By assigning `blob_ref = blob` when the new format blob is allocated, the memory is safely freed on all return paths, including early returns, without needing the manual conditional `kfree`. The old cleanup statement is removed to avoid double-free.

